From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:59:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement Phase C: squad-shared enemy memory + fix a decay
 bug

Per docs/designs/hybrid-ai-core-phase-c.md. Investigated CSquadMonster
first, per spec section 19: it already shares m_vecEnemyLKP and
"anyone in the squad has seen the enemy" timing through the leader
(SquadPasteEnemyInfo/SquadCopyEnemyInfo/m_flLastEnemySightTime), and
squad slots already provide role-like behavior - so this phase does
NOT reimplement a squad blackboard or role system. Its only new work:
teach the confidence model to distinguish direct sight from
squad-shared knowledge (spec section 8-9).

- dlls/ai_hybrid_core.h/.cpp: AIMemorySource enum (NONE/DIRECT_SIGHT/
  SQUAD_SHARED; HEARD/INFERRED deferred - no soundent integration
  yet), AI_CONFIDENCE_SQUAD_REPORT_FLOOR (0.7, per spec section 9).
  UpdateEnemyMemory()/DecideAction() take AIMemorySource instead of a
  bare enemyVisible bool. Squad-shared floors confidence at 0.7
  without lowering an already-higher (more recent direct-sight-
  derived) value. AIUtilityContext untouched - ScoreAttack still
  requires actual visibility, so squad-only knowledge can never
  trigger an attack, only SEARCH.
- Bug fix: UpdateEnemyMemory()'s decay anchor (lastSeenTime) was only
  advanced on a (re)sighting, not on every decay step, so repeated
  no-new-information ticks re-decayed an already-decayed value from a
  fixed, stale anchor - compounding decay incorrectly. This was live
  since Phase B (just not obviously wrong at a glance). Fixed by
  advancing the anchor on every call that computes decay; added a
  regression test asserting two sequential decay steps compose
  correctly.
- dlls/game.h/.cpp: new CVar ai_hybrid_squad_report_recency (default 5s).
- dlls/hgrunt.cpp: computes AIMemorySource from bits_COND_SEE_ENEMY /
  InSquad() / MySquadLeader()->m_flLastEnemySightTime (already kept
  current by this class's own pre-existing code and
  CSquadMonster::SquadMakeEnemy() - no new position/timing plumbing).
  Capability mask gains AI_CAP_SQUAD.

Verified: all core tests pass (including the new regression test),
client.so/vgui.so byte-identical to the pre-Phase-A baseline (only
hl.so differs). Manual in-game playtest of squad-sharing behavior is
still open.

